// Deal or Force - which house sits on which crown (DynastyCatalog.cs).
//
// A row is a house and the tags wearing it. Nothing here is state: it is the genealogy a
// claim reads. In 2024 no shared house is in crisis, so the dynastic casus belli sleeps;
// when a monarchy of one house falls into civil war or below the stability floor, a cousin
// crown acquires the oldest reason for a war there is, and the peace that ends it restores
// a personal union rather than annexing.
//
// A mod for an older age writes the houses of that age - Habsburg, Bourbon, Romanov,
// Piast - and the same two strings (dynastic_claim, personal_union) do the rest. That is
// the room-for-modders rule: the era lives in data, the mechanic in two seams.
{
  "dynasties": {
    "windsor": ["GBR", "CAN", "AUS", "NZL", "JAM", "BHS", "BRB", "PNG", "SLB", "TUV", "GRD", "LCA", "VCT", "ATG", "BLZ"],
